          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter 12 — How Nature Works in Harmony"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.888,
            0.029,
            0.922,
            0.044
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "199"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.092,
            0.551,
            0.117
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 12.6: Let us link (relate)"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.129,
            0.577,
            0.149
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Take an example of a grassland ecosystem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.154,
            0.743,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the following organisms that we can spot in a grassland ecosystem: grass, frog, hare, grasshopper, snake, and eagle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.215,
            0.743,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z In Fig. 12.8, a relationship of who eats whom is shown among some of the organisms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.257,
            0.742,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Draw",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the feeding relationships for the remaining organisms by adding arrows, similar to those in Fig. 12.8."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.301,
            0.743,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Fig 12.8, you can see that the grass is eaten by the hare and the hare is eaten by the leopard. This is a representation of a food chain in a grassland ecosystem. Which is another food chain that can be drawn for the organisms given in this activity? One example may be as follows:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.397,
            0.707,
            0.415
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grass Grasshopper Frog Snake Eagle"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.415,
            0.744,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The interactions between biotic components based on feeding relationships can be represented in the form of a linear chain. A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "food chain",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a simple sequence showing ‘who eats whom’ in an ecosystem. One such example is given in Fig. 12.9."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.761,
            0.084,
            0.94,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.761,
                0.084,
                0.94,
                0.57
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.51,
            0.465,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 12.7: Let us draw"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.551,
            0.742,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 12.10a represents a crop field with millets, mouse, and eagle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.575,
            0.726,
            0.594
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Count",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the number of each type of organism in Fig. 12.10a."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.598,
            0.744,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Make a table and set a number in the table against each of the organisms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.642,
            0.515,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Arrange the numbers in the ascending order, consider the highest number at the base and the lowest at the top."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.703,
            0.514,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Place the mouse, millet, and eagle appropriately in Fig. 12.10b."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.746,
            0.514,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What figure do you get? It looks like a pyramid. Complete the pyramid in Fig. 12.10b."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.808,
            0.515,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Each organism in a food chain has a specific position, called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "trophic level",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (troph = food):"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.866,
            0.515,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Producers (like green plants) are at the first trophic level."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.54,
            0.626,
            0.93,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 19,
              "bbox": [
                0.759,
                0.575,
                0.942,
                0.608
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 12.9: Another food chain in a grassland"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 21,
              "bbox": [
                0.54,
                0.626,
